   "answer": "On EPLB, the agent plateaued at a score of ∼0.21 for over 120 turns due to a refinement phase stuck because the code only allowed experts with two or more replicas to donate, which was too restrictive. The diagnosis identified this donor constraint as the bottleneck, and temporarily allowing an expert to give up its last replica broke the plateau, lifting the score from 0.21 to 0.23. [4:23]"
