   "answer": "The paper defines detecting co-dependent improvements as identifying when parameter changes only yield gains when applied together, which single-parameter sweeps miss. In IMG-100, the agent recognized AMP as a VRAM enabler: reducing memory from 14.3 GB to 4.1 GB made deeper architectures feasible, which in turn made CutMix augmentation beneficial and EMA stable, forming a chain of co-dependent gains (82.38%→84.03%) that collapsed if any link was removed [4:36]."
