    "total_tokens": 18251,
    "calls_tokens_unknown": 0
   },
   "answer": "The Inference Agent is restricted from accessing the Wiki Layer during training rollouts, as ablation shows that allowing wiki access during training negatively affects skill development [5:13]. When the Inference Agent has wiki access during training rollouts, average benchmark performance drops from 63.7% to 60.9%, with substantial declines on LiveMath (72.6% to 64.8%) [5:31]. This degradation occurs because the Inference Agent may obtain task-solving knowledge directly from the wiki rather than from skills, making trajectories less informative for skill development [5:31]. Conversely, disabling wiki access for the Inference Agent while providing it to the Skill Proposer increases performance from 48.7% to 63.7% (+15.0%) [5:30]."
  },
