   "answer": "WikiSkill uses statistical significance testing (specifically, paired t-tests or similar procedures) to report scores when benchmark validation splits are small, and handles statistically tied comparisons by declaring no significant difference when p-values exceed a threshold (typically p > 0.05), indicating that observed performance differences are not reliable given limited validation data. [5:57]"
